IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fca-nouns`
IMPORT `fca-definitions`
IMPORT `fca-s3-application`
IMPORT `fca-s2-adjustment`

-- Tests for section 2 of the Frustrated Contracts Act 1959.  Every expected value is written beside its assertion, from the text of the
-- Act, before the run.  A failing assertion is a finding, never an edit of the expected value.
--
-- Positional constructors; the rulers (fields in order):
--   Contract facts:  frustrated, discharged, discharge date, made, Government, charterparty, time charterparty, demise charterparty,
--                    carriage of goods by sea, insurance, SGA s 7 applies, specific goods, goods perished
--   Sum facts:       amount, was paid, in pursuance of the contract, before the discharge
--   Expenses facts:  incurred, amount, overhead sum the court includes, personal-work sum the court includes
--   Benefit facts:   obtained a valuable benefit, before the discharge, is a payment of money to which s 2(2) applies, value, sums retained or recoverable under s 2(3)
--   Obligor facts:   assumed obligations, in consideration of a benefit conferred on another person, that person is a party
--   Insurance facts: the court is considering a recovery or retention, sums have become payable under insurance, express term to insure, enactment to insure

§ `Fixtures`

`an ordinary frustrated contract` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract that is frustrated but whose parties have not been discharged` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING, Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract that is not frustrated` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a frustrated contract of insurance` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a frustrated contract discharged on 31 December 1958` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 31 12 1958), Date 1 1 1950, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a frustrated contract discharged on 1 January 1959` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 1 1959), Date 1 1 1950, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a frustrated contract discharged on a date not given` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, NOTHING, Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

`a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` MEANS
    `Sum facts` OF 1000, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a sum of 500 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` MEANS
    `Sum facts` OF 500, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a sum of 1000 paid under the contract after the discharge` MEANS
    `Sum facts` OF 1000, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a sum of 500 that fell payable after the discharge` MEANS
    `Sum facts` OF 500, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a sum of 1000 paid but not in pursuance of the contract` MEANS
    `Sum facts` OF 1000, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a sum of 200 paid under the contract before the discharge` MEANS
    `Sum facts` OF 200, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

`expenses of 300 with nothing added` MEANS
    `Expenses facts` OF TRUE, 300, 0, 0
`expenses of 300 with 50 for overhead and 25 for personal work` MEANS
    `Expenses facts` OF TRUE, 300, 50, 25
`no expenses incurred` MEANS
    `Expenses facts` OF FALSE, 0, 0, 0
`expenses of 2000 with nothing added` MEANS
    `Expenses facts` OF TRUE, 2000, 0, 0

`a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` MEANS
    `Benefit facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 5000, 100
`a valuable benefit obtained after the discharge` MEANS
    `Benefit facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 5000, 0
`no valuable benefit obtained` MEANS
    `Benefit facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, 0, 0
`a payment of money to which section 2(2) applies` MEANS
    `Benefit facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 5000, 0

§ `Tests -- s 2(1) when section 2 has effect`

-- text: "Where a contract has become impossible of performance or been otherwise frustrated, and the parties to the contract have for that reason been discharged from the further performance of the contract, this section shall, subject to section 3, have effect"
#ASSERT `s 2(1) section 2 has effect in relation to the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- each limb of the "where" not met: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) section 2 has effect in relation to the contract` `a contract that is not frustrated` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) section 2 has effect in relation to the contract` `a contract that is frustrated but whose parties have not been discharged` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "subject to section 3": s 3(5)(b) (insurance) and s 3(1) (discharged before 1 January 1959) say the Act does not apply
#ASSERT `s 2(1) section 2 has effect in relation to the contract` `a frustrated contract of insurance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) section 2 has effect in relation to the contract` `a frustrated contract discharged on 31 December 1958` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) section 2 has effect in relation to the contract` `a frustrated contract discharged on 1 January 1959` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not covered: the date of the time of discharge is not given, so s 3(1) cannot be applied
#ASSERT `s 2(1) section 2 has effect in relation to the contract` `a frustrated contract discharged on a date not given` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2(2) sums paid or payable`

-- text: "in the case of sums so paid, be recoverable from him as money received by him for the use of the party by whom the sums were paid"
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a sum paid is recoverable from the party who received it` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- text: "in the case of sums so payable, cease to be so payable"
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a sum payable ceases to be payable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 500 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- each limb reaches only its own kind of sum: NOTHING for the other kind
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a sum payable ceases to be payable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a sum paid is recoverable from the party who received it` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 500 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "before the time when the parties were so discharged": a time the text fixes in its own words, so a sum paid, or falling payable, after it is not one the subsection reaches (JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a); fork F2)
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a sum paid is recoverable from the party who received it` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract after the discharge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a sum payable ceases to be payable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 500 that fell payable after the discharge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "in pursuance of the contract": a sum paid otherwise is outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a sum paid is recoverable from the party who received it` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid but not in pursuance of the contract` EQUALS NOTHING
-- section 2 has no effect (not frustrated; insurance): JUST FALSE, carried from s 2(1)
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a sum paid is recoverable from the party who received it` `a contract that is not frustrated` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a sum payable ceases to be payable` `a frustrated contract of insurance` `a sum of 500 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not covered: whether section 2 has effect cannot be told
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a sum paid is recoverable from the party who received it` `a frustrated contract discharged on a date not given` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the defined term (s 2(2)): "the time of discharge" is the time the parties were so discharged
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the time of discharge` `an ordinary frustrated contract` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 6 2020)
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the time of discharge` `a contract that is frustrated but whose parties have not been discharged` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) there is a time of discharge` `an ordinary frustrated contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) there is a time of discharge` `a contract that is frustrated but whose parties have not been discharged` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) there is a time of discharge` `a frustrated contract discharged on a date not given` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the time of discharge` `a frustrated contract discharged on a date not given` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2(5) estimating expenses`

-- text: "the court may ... include such sum as appears to be reasonable in respect of overhead expenses and in respect of any work or services performed personally by that party"
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the expenses as estimated` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the expenses as estimated` `expenses of 300 with 50 for overhead and 25 for personal work` EQUALS JUST 375
-- not covered: no expenses incurred, nothing to estimate
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the expenses as estimated` `no expenses incurred` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the amount of the expenses as estimated, counting none incurred as 0` `no expenses incurred` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the amount of the expenses as estimated, counting none incurred as 0` `expenses of 300 with 50 for overhead and 25 for personal work` EQUALS 375
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the court may include a reasonable sum for overhead expenses and for work performed personally` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the court may include a reasonable sum for overhead expenses and for work performed personally` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `no expenses incurred` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the court may include a reasonable sum for overhead expenses and for work performed personally` `a contract that is not frustrated` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 2(3) retaining or recovering expenses`

-- text: "If the party ... incurred expenses ..., the court may, if it considers it just to do so ..., allow him to retain or ... recover the whole or any part of the sums"
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the court may allow the party to retain or recover the whole or part of the sums` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the first "if" not met: no expenses incurred -> JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the court may allow the party to retain or recover the whole or part of the sums` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `no expenses incurred` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the second "if" not met: the court does not consider it just -> JUST FALSE; not yet said -> NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the court may allow the party to retain or recover the whole or part of the sums` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the court may allow the party to retain or recover the whole or part of the sums` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- sums payable work the same way
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the court may allow the party to retain or recover the whole or part of the sums` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 500 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a sum paid after the discharge is not one of "the sums so paid or payable under subsection (2)": the same time bound, JUST FALSE (fork F2)
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the court may allow the party to retain or recover the whole or part of the sums` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract after the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- section 2 has no effect: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the court may allow the party to retain or recover the whole or part of the sums` `a contract that is not frustrated` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the ceiling: "not being an amount in excess of the expenses so incurred"; the whole or any part of the sums
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with 50 for overhead and 25 for personal work` EQUALS JUST 375
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 2000 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `no expenses incurred` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered` `a contract that is not frustrated` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` EQUALS NOTHING
-- an amount in fact allowed, on each side of the ceiling (300 on expenses of 300; sum 1000)
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` 300 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` 301 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with 50 for overhead and 25 for personal work` 375 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with 50 for overhead and 25 for personal work` 376 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an amount above the sums themselves (sum 200, expenses 300): over the sums but within the expenses -> NOTHING; over the expenses -> JUST FALSE; at the sums -> JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 200 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` 200 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 200 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` 250 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 200 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` 301 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not covered: no ceiling where the power is not available (no expenses)
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `no expenses incurred` 10 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2(2) with s 2(3): what is left`

-- sum paid 1000, expenses 300: the court allows 200 to be retained -> 800 recoverable; allows the ceiling 300 -> 700; allows nothing -> 1000
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum paid that is recoverable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 200) EQUALS JUST 800
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum paid that is recoverable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 300) EQUALS JUST 700
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum paid that is recoverable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 1000
-- the court does not consider it just, or there were no expenses: nothing is retained, the whole sum is recoverable
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum paid that is recoverable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum paid that is recoverable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `no expenses incurred` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 1000
-- not covered: the court has not said; an allowance above the ceiling; a sum s 2(2) does not make recoverable
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum paid that is recoverable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum paid that is recoverable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum paid that is recoverable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 301) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum paid that is recoverable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 500 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 100) EQUALS NOTHING
-- sum payable 500, expenses 200: the sum ceases to be payable; the court allows 150 to be recovered -> 150 remains payable; the court does not consider it just -> 0
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum payable that remains payable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 500 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 150) EQUALS JUST 150
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum payable that remains payable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 500 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum payable that remains payable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 500 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` `no expenses incurred` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum payable that remains payable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 500 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum payable that remains payable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 500 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 301) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subject to s 2(3) the amount of the sum payable that remains payable` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 100) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2(4) a valuable benefit`

-- text: "Where any party ... has ... obtained a valuable benefit (other than a payment of money to which subsection (2) applies) before the time of discharge, there shall be recoverable from him ... such sum (if any), not exceeding the value of that benefit"
#ASSERT `s 2(4) a sum is recoverable from the party who obtained a valuable benefit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the "where" not met: no benefit obtained; obtained after the discharge -> JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) a sum is recoverable from the party who obtained a valuable benefit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `no valuable benefit obtained` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) a sum is recoverable from the party who obtained a valuable benefit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a valuable benefit obtained after the discharge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "(other than a payment of money to which subsection (2) applies)": part of what the "Where" describes, so a payment to which s 2(2) applies is a "where" not met: JUST FALSE (judgment call QE)
#ASSERT `s 2(4) a sum is recoverable from the party who obtained a valuable benefit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a payment of money to which section 2(2) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- section 2 has no effect: JUST FALSE; cannot be told: NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(4) a sum is recoverable from the party who obtained a valuable benefit` `a contract that is not frustrated` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) a sum is recoverable from the party who obtained a valuable benefit` `a frustrated contract discharged on a date not given` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the ceiling: the value of the benefit to the party obtaining it
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the most that is recoverable for the valuable benefit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the most that is recoverable for the valuable benefit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `no valuable benefit obtained` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the sum the court considers just is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` 5000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the sum the court considers just is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` 5001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the sum the court considers just is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the sum the court considers just is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `no valuable benefit obtained` 10 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a): the benefited party's expenses (300 + 50 + 25 = 375) and the sums retained or recoverable under s 2(3) (100) -> 475; no expenses -> 100 only
#ASSERT `s 2(4)(a) the amount of the benefited party's expenses that the court has regard to` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` `expenses of 300 with 50 for overhead and 25 for personal work` EQUALS JUST 475
#ASSERT `s 2(4)(a) the amount of the benefited party's expenses that the court has regard to` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` `no expenses incurred` EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 2(4)(a) the amount of the benefited party's expenses that the court has regard to` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `no valuable benefit obtained` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the matters the court has regard to: (a), (b), any other circumstance of the case
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the court is to have regard to this matter` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` `the expenses incurred before the time of discharge by the benefited party (paragraph (a))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the court is to have regard to this matter` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` `the effect, in relation to that benefit, of the circumstances giving rise to the frustration of the contract (paragraph (b))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the court is to have regard to this matter` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` `some other circumstance of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the court is to have regard to this matter` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a valuable benefit worth 5000, with 100 retained under s 2(3)` `something that is not a circumstance of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the court is to have regard to this matter` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `no valuable benefit obtained` `some other circumstance of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the court is to have regard to this matter` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a payment of money to which section 2(2) applies` `some other circumstance of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Fixtures -- insurance and obligors`

`the court is considering recovery, insurance money paid, no duty to insure` MEANS
    `Insurance facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`the court is considering recovery, insurance money paid, an express term to insure` MEANS
    `Insurance facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`the court is considering recovery, insurance money paid, a duty to insure under an enactment` MEANS
    `Insurance facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`the court is considering recovery, no insurance money` MEANS
    `Insurance facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the court is not considering recovery, insurance money paid, no duty to insure` MEANS
    `Insurance facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

`a person who assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on a stranger` MEANS
    `Obligor facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a person who assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on a party` MEANS
    `Obligor facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`no one assumed obligations` MEANS
    `Obligor facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`obligations not assumed in consideration of a benefit` MEANS
    `Obligor facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 2(6) insurance money`

-- text: "the court shall not take into account any sums which have ... become payable to that party under any contract of insurance unless there was an obligation to insure imposed by an express term of the frustrated contract or by or under any enactment"
#ASSERT `s 2(6) the court shall not take the insurance sums into account` `the court is considering recovery, insurance money paid, no duty to insure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(6) the court may take the insurance sums into account` `the court is considering recovery, insurance money paid, no duty to insure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the "unless" is met (express term; enactment): the bar does not apply (JUST FALSE); the permission question is NOTHING (a lifted bar grants nothing; QA)
#ASSERT `s 2(6) the court shall not take the insurance sums into account` `the court is considering recovery, insurance money paid, an express term to insure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(6) the court may take the insurance sums into account` `the court is considering recovery, insurance money paid, an express term to insure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(6) the court shall not take the insurance sums into account` `the court is considering recovery, insurance money paid, a duty to insure under an enactment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(6) the court may take the insurance sums into account` `the court is considering recovery, insurance money paid, a duty to insure under an enactment` EQUALS NOTHING
-- other sums are outside the bar: NOTHING for both
#ASSERT `s 2(6) the court shall not take the insurance sums into account` `the court is considering recovery, no insurance money` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(6) the court may take the insurance sums into account` `the court is considering recovery, no insurance money` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "In considering whether any sum ought to be recovered or retained under this section": outside that consideration the bar is not engaged (JUST FALSE) and the Act is silent on a permission (NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 2(6) the court shall not take the insurance sums into account` `the court is not considering recovery, insurance money paid, no duty to insure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(6) the court may take the insurance sums into account` `the court is not considering recovery, insurance money paid, no duty to insure` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2(7) a benefit conferred on someone else`

-- text: "Where any person has assumed obligations under the contract in consideration of the conferring of a benefit by any other party to the contract upon any other person, whether a party to the contract or not, the court may, if ... it considers it just to do so, treat ... any benefit so conferred as a benefit obtained by the person who has assumed those obligations"
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the court may treat the benefit conferred on another person as a benefit obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a person who assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on a stranger` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "whether a party to the contract or not": the answer is the same
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the court may treat the benefit conferred on another person as a benefit obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a person who assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on a party` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the "where" not met -> JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the court may treat the benefit conferred on another person as a benefit obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `no one assumed obligations` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the court may treat the benefit conferred on another person as a benefit obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `obligations not assumed in consideration of a benefit` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the "if" not met: the court does not consider it just -> JUST FALSE; has not said -> NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the court may treat the benefit conferred on another person as a benefit obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a person who assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on a stranger` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the court may treat the benefit conferred on another person as a benefit obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a person who assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on a stranger` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- section 2 has no effect: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the court may treat the benefit conferred on another person as a benefit obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` `a contract that is not frustrated` `a person who assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on a stranger` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Fixtures -- the sums taken together`

`a sum of 2000 paid under the contract before the discharge` MEANS
    `Sum facts` OF 2000, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a sum of 3000 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` MEANS
    `Sum facts` OF 3000, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a sum of 9999 paid under the contract after the discharge` MEANS
    `Sum facts` OF 9999, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a sum of 9999 paid but not in pursuance of the contract` MEANS
    `Sum facts` OF 9999, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`2000 paid and 3000 payable` MEANS
    LIST `a sum of 2000 paid under the contract before the discharge`, `a sum of 3000 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid`
`3000 payable and 2000 paid` MEANS
    LIST `a sum of 3000 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid`, `a sum of 2000 paid under the contract before the discharge`
`1000 paid and 500 payable` MEANS
    LIST `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge`, `a sum of 500 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid`
`2000 paid and 3000 payable and 9999 paid after the discharge` MEANS
    LIST `a sum of 2000 paid under the contract before the discharge`, `a sum of 3000 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid`, `a sum of 9999 paid under the contract after the discharge`
`2000 paid and 3000 payable and 9999 paid but not in pursuance of the contract` MEANS
    LIST `a sum of 2000 paid under the contract before the discharge`, `a sum of 3000 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid`, `a sum of 9999 paid but not in pursuance of the contract`
`only sums that s 2(2) does not reach` MEANS
    LIST `a sum of 9999 paid under the contract after the discharge`, `a sum of 9999 paid but not in pursuance of the contract`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Sum facts`
`no sums at all` MEANS EMPTY

`expenses of 4000 with nothing added` MEANS
    `Expenses facts` OF TRUE, 4000, 0, 0
`expenses of 1000 with nothing added` MEANS
    `Expenses facts` OF TRUE, 1000, 0, 0
`expenses of 5000 with nothing added` MEANS
    `Expenses facts` OF TRUE, 5000, 0, 0
`expenses of 6000 with nothing added` MEANS
    `Expenses facts` OF TRUE, 6000, 0, 0
`expenses of 3000 with 500 for overhead and 500 for personal work` MEANS
    `Expenses facts` OF TRUE, 3000, 500, 500

§ `Tests -- s 2(3) the sums paid and the sums payable, taken together`

-- text: "the whole or any part of the sums so paid or payable ... not being an amount in excess of the expenses so incurred": ONE ceiling for the sums together
-- 2,000 paid and 3,000 payable (5,000 in all) against expenses of 4,000: 4,000
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST 4000
-- the order of the sums changes nothing: the total is a sum (fork F6)
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `3000 payable and 2000 paid` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST 4000
-- a total below the expenses (1,000 + 500 = 1,500 against 4,000): the total is the most
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `1000 paid and 500 payable` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST 1500
-- a total above the expenses (5,000 against 1,000): the expenses are the most
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 1000 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST 1000
-- a total equal to the expenses (5,000 and 5,000)
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 5000 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST 5000
-- expenses as estimated under s 2(5): 3,000 + 500 + 500 = 4,000
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 3000 with 500 for overhead and 500 for personal work` EQUALS JUST 4000
-- a sum paid after the discharge is not one of "the sums so paid or payable under subsection (2)": not counted
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable and 9999 paid after the discharge` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST 4000
-- a sum not paid in pursuance of the contract is not counted
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable and 9999 paid but not in pursuance of the contract` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST 4000
-- no sum that s 2(2) reaches: no total, so no ceiling
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `only sums that s 2(2) does not reach` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` EQUALS NOTHING
-- no sums given
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `no sums at all` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` EQUALS NOTHING
-- no expenses incurred: the power does not arise
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `no expenses incurred` EQUALS NOTHING
-- section 2 has no effect on a contract of insurance
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `a frustrated contract of insurance` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` EQUALS NOTHING
-- section 2 has no effect on a contract that is not frustrated
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `a contract that is not frustrated` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` EQUALS NOTHING
-- whether section 2 has effect cannot be told
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered from the sums taken together` `a frustrated contract discharged on a date not given` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the amount in fact allowed from the sums together, on each side of the ceiling (sums 2,000 + 3,000, expenses 4,000)
-- 4,000 equals the expenses
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows from the sums taken together is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` 4000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "in excess of the expenses so incurred"
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows from the sums taken together is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` 4001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- nothing allowed is within the limit
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows from the sums taken together is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 5,000 = the single-sum ceilings added (2,000 + 3,000) exceeds the expenses: the Act allows 4,000 in all
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows from the sums taken together is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` 5000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- expenses of 6,000 against sums of 5,000 in all: up to the sums is within the limit; above the sums, though within the expenses, is not any part of them
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows from the sums taken together is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 6000 with nothing added` 5000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows from the sums taken together is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 6000 with nothing added` 5001 EQUALS NOTHING
-- above the expenses as well
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows from the sums taken together is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `expenses of 6000 with nothing added` 6001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no expenses incurred: no ceiling
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows from the sums taken together is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `2000 paid and 3000 payable` `no expenses incurred` 10 EQUALS NOTHING
-- no sum that s 2(2) reaches: no ceiling
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows from the sums taken together is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `only sums that s 2(2) does not reach` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` 10 EQUALS NOTHING
-- the single-sum functions are as they were: each sum has its own ceiling (these two alone would let 2,000 + 3,000 = 5,000 through)
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 2000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST 2000
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the most the court may allow to be retained or recovered` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 3000 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST 3000
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 2000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` 2000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount the court allows is within the limit` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 3000 payable under the contract before the discharge and not paid` `expenses of 4000 with nothing added` 3000 EQUALS JUST TRUE

